<p>Early on the morning of the 3rd, we headed back to the airport for a flight to Chiloé, the location of the pre-program.</p>
<h2>Classes &amp; Activites</h2>
<p>The pre-program is a time to learn about Chilean culture and language (always intertwined) and to get to know the group before we head off to separate host families in Santiago. Last year the woman who ran it for 30+ years retired and Claudio took over, moving the program to his current home of Puchilco, a small town on an island in the Chiloé archipelago. Claudio researches and teaches indigenous culture in Chile, and has a lot of experience running programs for foreigners. We stayed in small cabins near the water, and spent most of our days either in the multi-purpose building nearby, taking classes and eating meals, or borrowing one of the local public-transportation buses to see more of the island and tour local farms.</p>
